["```javascript
import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';

const ComponentManager = ({ config }) => {
  const [components, setComponents] = useState({});

  useEffect(() => {
    const fetchComponentData = async (componentId) => {
      try {
        const response = await fetch(`/api/component/${componentId}`);
        if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Network response was not ok');
        const data = await response.json();
        setComponents((prevComponents) => ({
          ...prevComponents,
          [componentId]: data,
        }));
      } catch (error) {
        console.error(`Error fetching component ${componentId}:`, error);
      }
    };

    const debouncedFetchComponentData = debounce(fetchComponentData, 300);

    Object.keys(config).forEach((componentId) => {
      debouncedFetchComponentData(componentId);
    });

    return () => {
      // Cleanup any subscriptions or event listeners if necessary
    };
  }, [config]);

  const debounce = (func, wait) => {
    let timeout;
    return function(...args) {
      clearTimeout(timeout);
      timeout = setTimeout(() => func.apply(this, args), wait);
    };
  };

  return (
    <div>
      {Object.keys(components).map((componentId) => (
        <Component key={componentId} data={components[componentId]} />
      ))}
    </div>
  );
};

const Component = ({ data }) => {
  // Render the component based on the provided data
  return <div>{data.name}</div>;
};

export default ComponentManager;
```

This code snippet provides a basic implementation of a `ComponentManager` React component that dynamically updates a list of user interface components based on configuration parameters. It uses the `useState` and `useEffect` hooks to manage state and side effects, respectively. The `fetchComponentData` function is debounced using the `debounce` utility function to minimize unnecessary API calls when configuration changes occur frequently. Error handling is implemented to catch and log any errors that occur during asynchronous API requests. The component renders a list of child components based on the fetched data."]

